-.. method:: ModelAdmin.get_inline_instances(request, obj=None)
+.. method:: ModelAdmin.get_inlines(request, obj=None)
+
+    .. versionadded:: 3.2
+
+    The ``get_inlines`` method is given the ``HttpRequest`` and the
+    ``obj`` being edited (or ``None`` on an add form) and is expected to
+    return a ``list`` or ``tuple`` of :class:`~django.contrib.admin.InlineModelAdmin`
+    classes (not instances). It is used by :meth:`get_inline_instances` to
+    determine which inlines to use. This method allows you to customize
+    which inlines are displayed based on the request or the model instance.
+
+    For example, to return different inlines based on the request::
+
+        class MyModelAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
+            inlines = [MyInline, OtherInline]
+
+            def get_inlines(self, request, obj=None):
+                if obj and obj.is_premium:
+                    return self.inlines
+                return [self.inlines[0]]
+
